      {
        "id": 115246,
        "name": "Foote",
        "username": "Foote",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-08-18T20:48:51.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"truednd\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/truednd/48/2419_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> truednd:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>There was some contention yesterday when playing the first scenario and using Baron Blade's teleport movement power (I do not have the card currently with me, so I don't remember the exact name or the full wording of what the card says).Because it does state that Baron Blade can choose a spot within line of sight, if he were to stand at Elevation 4, could he teleport to any spot at elevation 3 and/or 4 using this movement ability? Obviously he can only do it one time per turn, but just looking for clarification because I do remember that it only states that LOS is required for the movement, but doesn't list the exact range.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yup thats right. He can port clear across the map depending on where he is standing. It's vital for Blade, and heros just have to be very aware of it.</p>",
